ed with people or things)\n \n/\n\napretado, incómodo (debido a estar apretado o abarrotado con personas o cosas)\n\nTwakni\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nthick, wide\n, dense\n \n/\n \ng\nrueso, ancho, espeso, denso\n\nTwaknika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthickness, width, density\n \n/ grosor, ancho, espesor, densidad\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-2\n \nKronikas\n \n3:3\n):\n \nplaya nani ba, yarika ba 90 pît bara twaknika ba 30 pît bri kan\n \n–\n \nthe foundation …, had a length\n\nof 90 feet and a width of 30 feet\n \n/\n \nlos cimientos …,\n \ntenía una longitud de 90 pies y un ancho de 30 pies)\n\nTwaku\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npipe\n \n/ tubo\n\nTwaku diaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto smoke\n \n/ fumar\n \nHow commonly is this used?\n\nTwaku samaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto chew...\n \nThis is used to translate\n \nchewing betel nut\n \nat\n \nbh127\n. See how it is commonly used.\n\nTwas\n \n(a/t:\n \nTauas\n,\n \nTwast\n,\n \nTawas\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \npapaya\n \n/ papaya\n\nTwatwilkra\n \n(see/ver:\n \nTwilkaia\n) (n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nmessenger, carrier, courier, transporter\n \n/ mensajero, transportista\n\nBîla twatwilkra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nmessenger, someone who carries a message\n \n/ mensajero, alguien que lleva\nun mensaje\n\nTwelp\n \n(\nmba-\n \nfrom English / de inglés)\n \n–\n \ntwelve\n \n/ doce\n\nTwi\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngrass, pasture, field\n \n/ hierba, pasto, campo\n\n(Construct:\n \nTwiya\n;\n \nTwaya\n-alt)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb70\n):\n \nSepad nani ba ai sîpka nani main kaikaia kli twi ra wan\n \n–\n \nThe shepherds went to the pasture again to watch their\nsheep\n \n/ Los pastores volvieron al campo para observar a sus ovejas)\n\nTwi bîla\n \n–\n \npath or way to a savannah, path or way to a field, path or way to a pasture\n \n/ camino a una sabana,\ncamino a un campo, camino a un pasto\n\nTwi irbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto chop grass, ........\n \n/ cortar hierba,\n \n........\n\nTwi kura\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngreen grass, young green grass, green vegetation\n \n/ pasto verde, hierba verde, hierba verde\n\ntierna\n, vegetaci\nó\nn verde\n\nTwi langni\n \n(v\n)\n \n–\n \nplain\n \n/ llano\n\nTwiura\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nTwiwra\n)\n \n–\n \nin the fields, in the countryside, in the savannah\n \n/ en los campos, en el campo, en la\n\nsabana\n\nTwilkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto carry on the back, to hold up, to support, to carry, to transport, to bear\n \n/ llevar sobre la espalda,\nsostener, transportar, soportar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-1 Korint 14:4\n):\n \nlatwan lâka kasak ba diara sut ba twilkisa\n \n–\n \ntrue love bears all things\n \n/ el verdadero amor lleva todo)",
